$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for N-Boc-Protected o-Aryl
Anilines. A mixture of N-Boc-protected o-bromoaniline 1 (1 equiv), the
corresponding boronic acid (1.6 equiv),
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium (5 mol %), and potassium carbonate
(2.5 equiv) in toluene/ EtOH (4/1) (0.1 M) was stirred at 80 °C under an
argon atmosphere for 2-4 h. The reaction mixture was diluted with AcOEt,
washed with water and brine, dried over MgSO4, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexanes/AcOEt) to afford the desired product. tert-Butyl
3-(2-((tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino)-4-fluorophenyl)-1H-pyrrole-1-carboxylate.
The product was obtained following the general procedure (3.0 mmol scale)
as an amorphous solid (915 mg, 81%) after purification by column
chromatography. Rf = 0.33 (5% AcOEt/hexanes); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.94 (d, J
= 11.7 Hz, 1H), 7.39-7.35 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.27 (m, 1H), 7.17 (dd, J = 8.5,
6.4 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (br s, 1H), 6.72 (ddd, J = 8.2, 8.2, 2.7 Hz, 1H), 6.31
(dd, J = 3.2, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 1.63 (s, 9H), 1.50 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ
162.4 (d, J = 225 Hz), 152.4, 148.5, 137.2 (d, J = 10.8 Hz), 130.7 (d, J
= 9.6 Hz), 123.1, 121.2, 119.6 (d, J = 2.4 Hz), 118.1, 112.5, 109.3 (d, J
= 21.6 Hz), 106.3 (d, J = 27.6 Hz), 84.3, 80.8, 28.2, 27.9; IR (neat)
3414, 2980, 1732, 1522, 1489, 1473, 1458, 1385, 1369 cm-1; MS (FAB) m/z
376 (M+), 320 (M -t-Bu), 264 (M -2t-Bu + H); HRMS-ESI (m/z) calcd for
C20H25FN2NaO4 399.1696, found 399.1703.
